  /Title (The above words refer to the talent. Basically the talent was the largest unit of weight in the ancient world, equal to about 34 kilograms (75 pounds). Later it was used as a monetary unit with a value that fluctuated, depending upon the particular monetary system that prevailed at a particular period of time. A silver talent was worth approximately 6000 denarii and a gold talent was worth at least thirty times that much.)
